# Policy: what a reader needs to check the paper is tracked -- the package that
# implements the oracle and the render protocol, the structures and labels it
# reads, the JSON record behind every reported number, and the released
# prediction vectors. Only regenerable state, caches, large binaries and the
# private development workspace are ignored.

# Private development workspace: the experiment drivers, the figure and table
# generators, the record prose, the manuscript sources and the agent
# instructions. Has its own README. Nothing here reaches the release.
/development/

# Trained adapters, distributed out of band for size. The manifest and sha256
# stay tracked in weights/README.md.
weights/*
!weights/README.md

# Rendered images: a build product. Five orthographic views per evaluation
# structure, a pure function of the CIFs and the frozen camera set that are
# tracked.
data/*/renders/

# Python bytecode, environments and tool caches (regenerable: `uv sync`)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
dist/
build/

# OS and editor junk
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
